# Mascot — Visual Design Brief

How the series mascot *looks*. Appearance only.

---

## Decided traits
These apply to every variant below.

- **Cute & cartoonish** — but not childish; must carry adult tone/language and deadpan delivery.
- **Simple** — few elements, easy to redraw and animate.
- **Hand-doll / puppet** base form (puppet cues: big expressive mouth, simple body, "held" posture).
- **Flat vector** render — crisp lines, flat color fills, no felt/fabric texture.
- **Reads at thumbnail size** — silhouette must survive as a small black blob.
- **Works on light + dark backgrounds.**

---

## Variants
Same decided traits, three takes. Concrete proposals below — react, tweak, or reject.

### Variant A — "Bit" · abstract blob-monster
- **Form:** rounded bean/egg body, no neck, stubby armless or two-nub sides. One big horizontal puppet mouth splits the lower third. Slight side tuft of "fuzz" (2–3 vector spikes) so silhouette isn't a plain oval.
- **Color:** warm coral/tangerine body, off-white mouth interior, single dark accent for eyes.
- **Signature detail:** the tuft + the oversized mouth — deadpan comes from tiny eyes over a huge mouth.
- **Why it works:** zero real-world baggage, most freedom, cleanest thumbnail blob. Feels most "original IP."
- **Risk:** generic if the tuft/color aren't distinctive enough.

### Variant B — "Fox" · recognizable animal
- **Candidate animal:** fox (clever/curious connotation, sharp silhouette). Owl = runner-up (wisdom, but overused for "smart AI"). Cat = too meme-y.
- **Form:** triangular ear silhouette is the whole recognizability play. Puppet body keeps it simple — head + small held body, big mouth under the snout.
- **Color:** muted rust/terracotta (not neon orange), cream muzzle + belly, dark ear tips.
- **Signature detail:** the two triangle ears — instantly readable even as a black blob.
- **Why it works:** instant relatability, strongest small-size silhouette of the three.
- **Risk:** "clever fox mascot" is well-trodden; needs a twist to not feel stock.

### Variant C — "Sock-bot" · object / soft-robot
- **Form:** a soft/plush robot done as a puppet — rounded rectangular head, single visor-eye band OR two dot eyes, puppet mouth as a slot/speaker grille. Antenna nub for silhouette.
- **Color:** soft slate/blue-grey body, one warm accent (mustard or teal) on antenna/visor so it's not cold.
- **Signature detail:** antenna + visor band; the warm accent is what keeps it friendly not corporate.
- **Why it works:** on-theme for AI literacy, "AI as a helpful little device."
- **Risk:** closest to generic-AI-mascot cliché; leans cold unless the puppet cuteness is pushed hard.

